WEBVTT

00:00:04.349 --> 00:00:11.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the third of August. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the mime act again?</v>

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:18.500
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, got you. Only just made it in, mind. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid.</v>

00:00:19.429 --> 00:00:23.980
<v Jamie Brennan>You sound like you're still recovering from the walk across the car park.</v>

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:34.420
<v Callum Reid>I stopped to look at someone's new car in the car park, actually. That shiny blue one. Bit smarter than our usual collection.</v>

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.880
<v David Whitfield>Not mine. Mine's the one held together by road dirt.</v>

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:48.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get onto cars properly—tested the main isolation valve yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.799
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. So that one's closed, then?</v>

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.229
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, finished. Nothing further on that.</v>

00:00:54.750 --> 00:01:02.450
<v Hannah Price>And I signed off the inspection on the line 1 mould temp on Tuesday. That's done as well, just for the record.</v>

00:01:04.829 --> 00:01:08.680
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, that one's showing closed. We're not carrying it into today.</v>

00:01:10.209 --> 00:01:15.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona Doyle, can you send the shift handover report round next Tuesday? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.269
<v Fiona Doyle>The existing handover report, yeah? Not a new format?</v>

00:01:20.959 --> 00:01:25.859
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, the existing one. Just get that round next Tuesday; it's fairly important.</v>

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.980
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, I'll send the shift handover report round next Tuesday.</v>

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:38.040
<v Callum Reid>While we're on where things stand, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line 3. Still blocked.</v>

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:44.810
<v Jamie Brennan>No, there's no confirmed date in what we've had back. Same position as before.</v>

00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:50.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That's a blocker update, then, not another chase we're allocating this morning.</v>

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:57.930
<v Fiona Doyle>Also, the shutdown on the fire panel is cancelled now, production need it running. That shutdown's off the plan.</v>

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:05.849
<v Priya Raman>Right. The shutdown, specifically—not the same thing as a function test on the fire alarm panel.</v>

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:16.449
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, so I'll run a function test on the fire alarm panel by end of day. That's the 'if you've got a spare minute' one, isn't it?</v>

00:02:18.949 --> 00:02:25.949
<v Sarah Okafor>It is, Cal. By end of day, but keep it at that spare-minute priority. We're not bringing the shutdown back.</v>

00:02:26.969 --> 00:02:30.819
<v Callum Reid>Yep, I'll do the function test on that basis. No shutdown.</v>

00:02:32.479 --> 00:02:38.780
<v Priya Raman>Got you. Two different things. Teams clipped the start of that and I thought we'd reversed the cancellation.</v>

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:46.189
<v David Whitfield>Um, just an observation from me: heard a slight rattle from the forklifts, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:02:48.229 --> 00:02:51.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observation only. Not putting a job against that.</v>

00:02:53.349 --> 00:02:56.849
<v David Whitfield>Exactly. Just mentioning what I heard, not calling a fault.</v>

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:07.830
<v Sarah Okafor>We do still need someone to grease and check the bearings on the GT1 Compressor Section by 11am. Normal priority. Anyone got room for that?</v>

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.259
<v David Whitfield>I haven't got room for it, sorry.</v>

00:03:12.069 --> 00:03:14.520
<v Callum Reid>Nor me. Can't honestly take that one.</v>

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone else able to pick up those bearings?</v>

00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:22.780
<v Priya Raman>Not me, I'm afraid. I can't take that on.</v>

00:03:23.479 --> 00:03:26.280
<v Fiona Doyle>That's still unallocated, then. No name against it.</v>

00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:34.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah. GT1 Compressor Section bearings stay unowned. The requirement is still by 11am, normal priority, but nobody's accepted it.</v>

00:03:35.349 --> 00:03:39.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, can you swap the filter on the IM1 hydraulic unit tomorrow morning?</v>

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:47.969
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I can do that. I'll swap the filter on the IM1 hydraulic unit tomorrow morning.</v>

00:03:49.039 --> 00:03:53.240
<v David Whitfield>That's just the filter change, rather than anything wider on the unit?</v>

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Just the filter change, yes.</v>

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:59.939
<v Hannah Price>Fine, that's what I've got. Tomorrow morning.</v>

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:08.039
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, I'll chase the purchase order for the water booster Monday. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:08.969 --> 00:04:13.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie. Monday being today, just so we're all on the same page?</v>

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:20.339
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, today, Monday. I'll chase the purchase order. Important enough, but not an urgent one.</v>

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:26.550
<v Fiona Doyle>And that's separate from the blocked line 3 delivery we just mentioned?</v>

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.529
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, completely separate. The water booster purchase order is the one I'm taking.</v>

00:04:35.629 --> 00:04:40.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah Price, can you investigate the pressure drop on the AC1 on Friday?</v>

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:44.459
<v Hannah Price>Yes, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the AC1 on Friday.</v>

00:04:46.399 --> 00:04:49.199
<v Callum Reid>Sorry—Friday, not being pulled into today's jobs, then?</v>

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, on Friday. Not today.</v>

00:04:54.019 --> 00:04:57.170
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's fine. I've got Friday for that investigation.</v>

00:04:57.629 --> 00:05:02.180
<v David Whitfield>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the booster pump after lunch.</v>

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:06.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Davey. Top priority please, that risk assessment.</v>

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.279
<v David Whitfield>Understood. I'll update it after lunch, top priority.</v>

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:18.319
<v Priya Raman>That's the assessment for the work, yeah—not saying the physical work's happening after lunch?</v>

00:05:19.279 --> 00:05:24.180
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, just updating the risk assessment. I'm not booking in the actual pump work.</v>

00:05:24.519 --> 00:05:29.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Sorry, we talked over each other there, but I think we've got that straight.</v>

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:37.959
<v Fiona Doyle>And mine's next Tuesday for sending the shift handover report round. I've kept your 'fairly important' against it.</v>

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, exactly.</v>

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:49.060
<v Callum Reid>I've got the fire alarm panel function test as the spare-minute one, by end of day. Not the cancelled shutdown.</v>

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.410
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep. Shutdown remains cancelled; production need it running.</v>

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:58.329
<v Hannah Price>Mine are clear: IM1 hydraulic unit filter tomorrow morning, AC1 pressure-drop investigation on Friday.</v>

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:05.329
<v Jamie Brennan>And water booster purchase order chase Monday, today. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:06:07.379 --> 00:06:10.879
<v David Whitfield>Booster pump risk assessment after lunch, top priority. Got it.</v>

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:15.689
<v Fiona Doyle>Only gap is the GT1 Compressor Section bearings. Still nobody taking that.</v>

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:22.610
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. Still needed by 11am at normal priority, but unowned. Let's not pretend we've covered it.</v>

00:06:24.569 --> 00:06:30.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, thanks all. That's us. And whoever owns that blue car, brave choice parking it here.</v>
